## Submitter Decision Guide

### Exact live-form verdict mapping

| Internal assessment | Main analysis field | Validity required | Duplicate analysis |
| ------------------- | ------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------ |
| Valid as-is | Valid as-is | Valid-as-is | Valid-as-is |
| Fixable | Fixable | Fixable | Fixable |
| Not Fixable | Invalid/Not Fixable | Invalid | Invalid/Not Fixable |

First and duplicate analysis answers must match semantically. Never emit “Not Fixable” for the internal radio when the available label is “Invalid.”

### Submitter quick checklist (ZIP workflow — read-only)

- [ ] ZIP identified; task root located; format classified (Current / Legacy / Hybrid / Unknown)
- [ ] Platform metadata verified against `task.toml` / repo / languages / source (mismatches reported; task not edited)
- [ ] Session times tracked internally (no session file on disk); times not invented
- [ ] Complete read-only audit finished; no task files modified
- [ ] Instruction↔test maps built; f2p count applied correctly (exactly 10 ≠ “less than 10”; “more than 10” only if ≥11)
- [ ] Internal assessment chosen for the **original** task; mapped to the three live form fields
- [ ] Conditional path fields prepared (Valid as-is / Fixable / Not Fixable); Fixable = analysis only
- [ ] All paste-ready answers delivered **in chat only** (do not create `sentinel_*.md` / `sentinel_*.txt` / session JSON)
- [ ] No corrected ZIP created; Files Changed = None

Full procedure: `.cursor/rules/Sentinel_Submitter_Platform_Workflow.mdc`.

### Valid as-is

Use when **no meaningful task defect is found** from available evidence (alignment, f2p count per operational rule below, no leakage, clear/non-prescriptive instruction, and validation evidence from inspection/logs when available).

**Examples:** Instruction, tests, and golden solution already match the PR; coverage/faithfulness solid; packaging clean.

### Fixable

Use when **defects exist but could theoretically be repaired within allowed files**. Do **not** repair them in Cursor Submitter Mode.

**Examples:** Over-prescriptive or LLM-like instruction; coverage gaps; **fewer than 10** f2p tests; `solution.patch` naming; missing `problem_statement.md` sync; allowed Dockerfile/git hygiene issues; natural PR-scope expansion that would be needed for difficulty.

### Not Fixable

Use only for **prohibited PR-scope changes** or **genuinely disallowed environment problems**.

**Examples:** Must shrink/replace the PR to make the task valid; tangled toolchain; large model download; required live external service; unrecoverable Git corruption.

**Legacy map:** Valid with no changes ≈ Valid as-is; Invalid minor/major ≈ Fixable when theoretically correctable; Invalid → Not Fixable only if current Not Fixable criteria hold.

