## Instruction Checklist

- [ ] Describes the problem and expected behavior
- [ ] Has measurable success criteria
- [ ] Is self-contained
- [ ] Does not disclose implementation steps
- [ ] Does not name hidden tests or verifier internals
- [ ] Does not expose PR details to the agent
- [ ] States required public schemas and formats
- [ ] Matches the source PR (plus any allowed expansion)
- [ ] Sounds like real engineering communication
- [ ] Does not require arbitrary guessing

A correct public output schema is **necessary** and is **not** leakage.

---

## Fail-to-Pass Count (Operational)

- **Official guideline minimum:** at least **10** meaningful fail-to-pass tests.
- Plain wording: At least 10 meaningful fail-to-pass tests.
- **Fixable test-count defect:** fewer than **10** fail-to-pass tests.
- **Exactly 10:** meets the documented guideline — not automatically Fixable.
- **Live-form “More than 10”:** select only when the original task already has ≥11; never claim it for exactly 10; do **not** add tests in Cursor Submitter Mode.
- **Preferred practical range:** **11–20** meaningful fail-to-pass tests.
- Plain wording: 11–20 meaningful fail-to-pass tests.
- Never add filler/duplicate/shallow tests only to raise the count.

Checkbox rules:

- 9 or fewer → select **“Less than 10 fail-to-pass tests in the test suite.”** and assess Fixable (report only; do not add tests).
- Exactly 10 → do **not** select “Less than 10.”
- Confirmation **“More than 10 fail-to-pass tests in the test suite”** → only when true for the original task.

