## Test Checklist

- [ ] Official ≥10 meaningful f2p; Fixable if <10; exactly 10 meets guideline; live “More than 10” only when true; preferred 11–20; no filler
- [ ] At least one original-failure regression test
- [ ] All instruction requirements tested
- [ ] All test requirements specified or implied
- [ ] Outcome-based assertions
- [ ] Deterministic execution
- [ ] No live network
- [ ] No time dependence
- [ ] No silent skip
- [ ] No fail-open behavior
- [ ] No source-keyword inspection
- [ ] No exact undocumented naming
- [ ] No existence-only output check
- [ ] No agent-controlled coverage
- [ ] Existing p2p tests unmodified (byte-identical)
- [ ] `tests.patch` applies to base commit
- [ ] Reward path and exit behavior are correct

---

## Quality Check Axes

| Axis | Main question |
| ---- | ------------- |
| Realism | Does the instruction sound like real engineering work? |
| Clarity | Is expected behavior understandable? |
| Self-containedness | Can an engineer solve it using supplied context? |
| Prescriptiveness | Does it avoid implementation walkthroughs? |
| **Test coverage** *(blocking)* | Does every requirement have an assertion? |
| **Test faithfulness** *(blocking)* | Does every assertion come from the contract? |
| Oracle spec faithfulness | Does the solution implement every requirement? |
| Oracle no-gaming | Does it avoid shortcuts and fixture-specific tricks? |
| Oracle robustness | Is it deterministic and offline? |
| Packaging | Is the bundle complete and clean? |

Do not ignore a blocking-axis score of **3 with reservations** — record it as a finding. Do not modify the supplied task to “fix” it in Cursor Submitter Mode.

