## Theoretical Fixable Components (Analysis Only)

In Cursor Submitter Mode, the matrix below describes components that are **theoretically correctable** for Fixable classification. It does **not** authorize edits.

| Component | Theoretically fixable? | Cursor Submitter Mode |
| --------- | ---------------------- | --------------------- |
| `instruction.md` | Yes | Report only — do not rewrite |
| `problem_statement.md` | Yes | Report only — do not sync/edit |
| `tests.patch` | Yes | Report only — do not add tests |
| Existing repo tests | No | Must remain unchanged |
| `test.sh` | Yes | Report only |
| `config.json` | Yes | Report only |
| `grade.py` | Yes | Report only |
| `solve.sh` | Yes | Report only |
| `golden.patch` / `solution.patch` | Yes | Report naming/content issues only — do not rename or edit |
| Dockerfile | Limited | Report only |
| Git metadata | Yes | Report only — do not clean |
| Tracked repo source | No | Never alter starting code |

PR scope may be **theoretically expandable** for difficulty; never reduce or replace it. In Cursor Submitter Mode, describe that expansion as a finding only — do not update instruction, tests, or oracle.

