## Git Quick Checks

Run inside `environment/repo`:

```bash
git rev-parse --verify HEAD                   # must succeed
git rev-parse HEAD                            # == base_commit_sha (HEAD wins if mismatch)
git rev-list --all --not HEAD                 # MUST be empty
git remote                                    # MUST be empty
git config --local --get-regexp '^filter\.'   # MUST be empty
git status --porcelain                        # MUST be empty
ls .git/logs 2>/dev/null                      # MUST NOT exist / empty
du -sh .git                                   # MUST be < 100 MB
git apply --check ../../tests/tests.patch     # MUST apply cleanly
```

Blank output is expected for several hygiene commands (`rev-list`, `remote`, `filter`, `status`). Git problems are usually **Fixable**, not automatically Not Fixable. In Cursor Submitter Mode, report Git findings only — do not clean or rewrite Git metadata in the supplied task.

