## Platform Eval Note (Quick)

In-app platform checks have a **five-minute** runtime limit. Iterate with Send to Reviewer unchecked when longer evaluation is needed; use local validation or downloaded logs. Do not claim a platform run completed if it stopped on the runtime limit.

---

## Agent Runs (Quick)

- Inspect **all** failing trials, not one convenient trial
- Confirm at least **one passing** trial when available
- Use logs for timeouts, systematic misreads, instability
- **Historical note:** older packages often have several trials per model; newer batches (e.g. from April 28 2026) may have fewer (often two — one per model). Smaller newer sets are expected, not automatically defective

A failing agent does **not** automatically prove the task is valid.

---

## Writing Guidance

- Keep notes simple, specific, and human
- Cite real file names, tests, functions, logs, and paths
- Number issues (Issue 1, Issue 2, …) with category + fixability + how to fix
- Vague write-ups get Needs Revision / Reject on older forms

---

## Oracle Notes (Quick)

- Extra oracle behavior alone is **not** a defect when required behavior is implemented and tests enforce it
- Unrelated refactors / drive-by edits should be removed
- No hardcoding, no reading hidden test ground truth, no live network, fixed seeds

A passing oracle does **not** automatically prove tests are complete.

